          <li id="fn2">Michael Polanyi's concept of tacit knowledge—"we know more than we can tell"—comes from <em>The Tacit Dimension</em> (1966). I extend this by distinguishing between tacit-because-costly and potentially-irreducibly-tacit knowledge.</li>
